Kubernetes Labels and Selectors

1️What are Labels in Kubernetes

	A Label is a key-value pair attached to Kubernetes objects.

	Labels help to identify, organize, and group resources.

	Commonly labeled resources:

		Kubernetes Pods

		Deployments

		Services

		Nodes

		ReplicaSets

		Namespaces

	Example Label
		labels:
		  app: nginx
		  env: production
		  tier: frontend

	Why Labels are Important

	Labels Are Used For:

		1️Grouping resources

		Example:

			All frontend pods
			All backend pods
			All production workloads

		2️Service Discovery

			Services route traffic using labels.

	
	Label Example (Pod)

		apiVersion: v1
		kind: Pod
		metadata:
		  name: nginx-pod
		  labels:
		    app: nginx
		    env: prod
		spec:
		  containers:
		  - name: nginx
		    image: nginx

		This pod has two labels:

		app = nginx
		env = prod


