What are Selectors

	A Selector is used to select objects based on labels.

	Selectors help Kubernetes find matching resources.

	Example use cases:

	Services find pods

	Deployments manage pods

	ReplicaSets scale pods

What are Selectors

	A Selector is used to select objects based on labels.

	Selectors help Kubernetes find matching resources.

	Example use cases:

	Services find pods

	Deployments manage pods

	ReplicaSets scale pods

Types of Selectors
	1️Equality-based Selector

Uses:

	=
	==
	!=
check the lables 

	kubectl get pods -l app=nginx

will print other lables 

	kubectl get pods -l env!=prod


Labels with Services (Important)

	Services use selectors to route traffic.

Pod:

apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata:
  name: nginx
  labels:
    app: web # labels

Service:

apiVersion: v1
kind: Service
metadata:
  name: web-service
spec:
  selector:
    app: nginx   # selector
  ports:
  - port: 80

Flow:

	Client Request
	      ↓
	Service
	      ↓
	Selector (app=web)
	      ↓
	Matching Pods


============================================================================

Show labels:

	kubectl get pods --show-labels

Filter pods:
	kubectl get pods -l app=web

Add label to running pod:

	kubectl label pod nginx env=prod

Remove label:

	kubectl label pod nginx env-


To check the labels
 
 kubectl describe pod <pod-name> -n <Name-space>

How to display only labels?

	kubectl get po <pod-name> -n <Name-space> --show-labels

How to see node and pod ip?
---------------------------

	kubectl get po -n test-ns -o wide

How to go inside of pod?
-------------------------

	kubectl exec -it -n test-ns <podname> -- sh

